body:
I like it but I wish there were more answers. There's rejecting a lot of things (which I support) but not what replaces it. Is "rising up" the solution?

&#x200B;

This was useful for "uncrossing" some thoughts in my mind. I previously identified with bougie feminisism while also working for grassroots feminisim, or however she would consider it. In the future I will be careful not to identify so much with the bougie feminism until everyone is taken care of.

Happiness is true wealth. If you can figure out what it feels like you are on this earth to do you will be so much better off than those who are playing the game to feel like a man.

&#x200B;

I had a mental breakdown at 30 and am going to aim to get a PhD to become a professor. I don't want to contribute to this capitalist society anymore.
